    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0484" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.15/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to J. P. Morgan
                        &amp; Co.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-18">June 18, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your letter
                    of June 13 referring to the possibility of participation by American interests
                    in financing in China.</p>
                <p>It is believed that, with regard to the China Consortium, the views of the
                    Department have been adequately expressed by Mr. Hornbeck <pb facs="0485"
                        n="395" xml:id="pg395"/> in the telephone conversation held between Mr.
                    Lamont and Mr. Hornbeck today.</p>
                <p>Referring to the views expressed in the concluding sentence of your letter, the
                    Department concurs.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
